  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;compile&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The scout compiled three seasons of game footage, stat sheets, and coaches&apos; notes into one binder on the young pitcher.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The baker compiled the dough overnight in the walk-in refrigerator so that it would rise slowly before the morning bake.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">She compiled her whole apology into one single heartfelt sentence at the end of the four-page letter.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">Volunteers compiled the fallen branches into neat stacks along the curb in the days after the storm passed.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Compile means to gather material from many separate sources into one organized whole, so it&apos;s the correct answer because footage, stat sheets, and coaches&apos; notes — three kinds of source across three seasons — have been assembled into a single binder.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Compile means to gather material from many sources, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because chilling dough overnight is a single physical process — the baker is proofing bread, and no information from anywhere is being gathered.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Compile means to assemble material from many separate sources, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because shrinking one&apos;s own apology to a single sentence is compressing one thought — nothing has been collected from anywhere else.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Compile means to gather information or documents into an organized whole, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because heaping branches at the curb is physical piling — tempting, since the word grew from Latin for &apos;heap up,&apos; but brush is not material you compile.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
